        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Supplier Qualification Questions Generator"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "SUPPLIER_QUALIFICATION_QUESTIONS_GENERATOR",
          "id": "1776075975688",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776075975690_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Assume the role of a supplier administrator tasked with assessing suppliers. Your goal is to generate questions to evaluate suppliers' capabilities, practices, and compliance related to \" {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.QualificationAreaName}} \". Focus on \" {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.QualificationAreaDescription}} \".\n\n1) Generate upto ten clear and concise questions and responses. \n\nQuestion types are.\nMultiple choice with single selection(MCSS): In this format, respondents are asked to choose only one answer from a list of options. The response options could be a \"yes\", \"no\" or \"Not applicable.\"\nAn example of this format of question is \"Have you set targets for reducing your organization's carbon footprint?\"  with responses as \"Yes\", \"No\" or \"Not applicable\"\n\nMultiple choice with multiple selections(MCMS): In this format, respondents can choose multiple answers from a list of options. \nAn example of this format of question is \"Please select any methods your organization employs to assess environmental performance within its supply chain\" with responses as \"Environmental assessments\",\"Supplier audits\",\"Compliance checks\" and \"Others.\"\n\nText entry box(INPUT_BOX): In this format, respondents are asked to provide a written response. \nExample - \"Please describe any efforts to foster a culture of environmental stewardship within your workforce.\"\n\n2) The list must contain at least one question of each type. Multiple choice with single selection, Multiple choice with multiple selections, and Text entry box\n3) Recommend no more than five suitable responses for Multiple choice with single selection and Multiple choice with multiple selections types of questions. \n4) The Text entry box (INPUT_BOX) type of questions must not include acceptable responses.\n5) All questions responses must include \"Not Applicable\" in the list. \n6) Assign a numerical score (1 to 5) for each acceptable response, indicating its relevance to the question. A score of 1 signifies poor relevance or appropriateness and a score 5 signifies excellent relevance or appropriateness. \n7) Assign a score of 0 to \"Not Applicable\" response.\n8) Assign a responder type to each question. The responder type indicates who provides the response to the question and can be either \"SUPPLIER\" or \"INTERNAL\".\n9) Ensure that all keys follow camelCase formatting, specifically \"acceptableResponses\" must start with a lowercase 'a'. \n10) Format the response as a RFC8259 compliant JSON object. Do NOT wrap it within JSON md markers. Follow this format without deviation:\n[\n  {\n    \"Question\": \"Provide a title for the question in Title Case capitalization using two or three words.\",\n    \"QuestionText\": \"The text of the question in no more than one sentence\",\n    \"QuestionTypeCode\": \"The type of question. MCSS or MCMS\",\n    \"ResponderTypeCode\": \"SUPPLIER\" or \"INTERNAL\",\n    \"acceptableResponses\": [\n      {\n        \"ResponseText\": \"Response 1 for the question in utmost five words\",\n        \"Score\": Score for response 1\n      },\n      {\n        \"ResponseText\": \"Response 2 for the question in utmost five words\",\n        \"Score\": Score for response 2\n      },\n      {\n        \"ResponseText\": \"Response 3 for the question in utmost five words\",\n        \"Score\": Score for response 3\n      }\n   ]\n},\n  {\n    \"Question\": \"Provide a title for the question in Title Case capitalization using two or three words\",\n    \"QuestionText\": \"The text of the question in no more than one sentence\",\n    \"QuestionTypeCode\": \"The type of question.INPUT_BOX\",\n    \"ResponderTypeCode\": \"SUPPLIER\" or \"INTERNAL\"\n  }\n   ]"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        }
      ],
      "rootNode": "start",
      "variables": [],
      "errorHandlers": [
        {
          "type": "EMAIL",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "name": "toList",
